    "content": "app/src/main/java/com/romankozak/forwardappmobile/features/mainscreen/MainScreenLayout.kt - головний екран\napp/src/main/java/com/romankozak/forwardappmobile/features/daymanagement/ui/DayManagementScreen.kt - це композабл який показується в вкладці Today головного екрану\napp/src/main/java/com/romankozak/forwardappmobile/features/mainscreen/bottompanels/TodayBottomPanel.kt - нижня панель вводу вкладки Today\napp/src/main/java/com/romankozak/forwardappmobile/features/missions/presentation/LinkedTargetsPickerDialog.kt - може бути корисним, а може ні\napp/src/main/java/com/romankozak/forwardappmobile/features/daymanagement/ui/dayplan/scopelinks/DayScopeLinksSheet.kt - схоже що тут аркуш який показується коли Today є активною вкладкою\n\nякщо тепнути по кнопці панелі вводу внизу з'явиться аркуш зв'язків. Inside TodayBottomPanel, there is a button that triggers a connection sheet.\n\nТой аркуш показує ConnectionsPanel вміст якої прив'язаний до ПОТОЧНОГО ДНЯ. тобто один день - один вміст панелі зв'язків. другий день - другий вміст. завдання в тому щоб зробити щоб вміст панелі зв'язків був прив'язаний не до дня конкретного дня а до вкладки Today семантично і технічно. тобто один зміст панелі зв'язків вкладки Today незалежно від того який день в нижній панелі активний. \n\n Connection sheet invocation: The sheet is triggered by the onShowContextMarkersSheet callback passed to           \n ▎  TodayBottomPanel when the active route is MAIN_SCREEN_TODAY_ROUTE. The button inside TodayBottomPanel likely      \n ▎  calls this callback, which presumably invokes dayPlanViewModel.toggleScopeLinksSheet() or similar.                \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎  Day‑specific binding: The sheet’s content is currently tied to the current day because dayPlanViewModel           \n ▎  (injected into DayManagementScreen) holds the dayPlanId for the selected day. The LinkedTargetsPickerDialog       \n ▎  likely uses that dayPlanId to fetch the connections for that specific day.                                        \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎  To make the connections panel independent of the selected day and instead bind it to the “Today” tab              \n ▎  semantically, you would need to:                                                                                  \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎   1 Change the source of the dayPlanId used by the sheet—perhaps use a fixed identifier for the “Today” tab        \n ▎     rather than the currently selected day’s plan.                                                                 \n ▎   2 Adjust the view‑model logic that fetches connections to rely on a tab‑specific scope instead of the          ▂ \n ▎     day‑specific dayPlanId.                                                                                        \n ▎                     \n\n  ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎   • The DayPlanViewModel has a connectionsOrder state and an updateConnectionsOrder function, indicating that      \n ▎     the order of connections is managed per day plan.                                                              \n ▎   • The UI component ConnectionsPanel is used in multiple screens (StrategicManagementScreen,                      \n ▎     MainBeaconEditorSheet, StrategicArcScreen, CoreScopeLinksSheet, DayScopeLinksSheet,                            \n ▎     TacticalScopeLinksSheet, ConnectionsView).      \n\n\n                                                                                                                \n ▎  The connections sheet (DayScopeLinksSheet) currently receives a DayPlanUiState that contains a dayPlan with       \n ▎  linkedProjectIds and linkedAttachmentIds. This uiState is built by DayPlanViewModel, which is scoped to a         \n ▎  specific dayPlanId (the currently selected day). That’s why the sheet’s content changes when you switch days.     \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎  To make the sheet independent of the selected day and bound to the “Today” tab semantically and technically,      \n ▎  you would need to:                                                                                                \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎   1 Change the source of the dayPlanId used by the sheet – instead of using the currently selected day’s           \n ▎     dayPlanId, use a fixed identifier that represents the “Today” tab scope (e.g., a special constant like         \n ▎     TODAY_TAB_SCOPE_ID or a null/empty value that the backend interprets as “today’s connections”).                \n ▎   2 Adjust the view‑model logic – either:                                                                          \n ▎      • Create a separate TodayTabConnectionsViewModel that manages connections for the “Today” tab                 \n ▎        independently of any specific day, or                                                                       \n ▎      • Extend DayPlanViewModel to support two modes: a day‑specific mode (for the day‑plan screen) and a           \n ▎        tab‑specific mode (for the “Today” tab). The mode would be determined by the caller (e.g.,                  \n ▎        TodayBottomPanel would request the tab‑specific mode).                                                      \n ▎   3 Update the UI layer – modify DayScopeLinksSheet (or create a new sheet) to accept a uiState that is not        \n ▎     tied to a dayPlan but to a tab‑scope. The sheet would then fetch connections based on the tab‑scope            \n ▎     identifier rather than dayPlanId.                                                                              \n ▎   4 Propagate the change through the navigation stack – ensure that the callback that triggers the sheet           \n ▎     (onShowContextMarkersSheet in TodayBottomPanel) uses the tab‑scoped view‑model or passes the correct scope     \n ▎     parameter to DayPlanViewModel.                                                                                 \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎  Next steps for a concrete implementation:                                                                         \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎   • Examine DayPlanViewModel.kt to see how toggleScopeLinksSheet works and how uiState is built.                 ▆ \n ▎   • Look at TodayBottomPanel.kt to see how the sheet is invoked.                                                   \n ▎   • Determine whether a new view‑model is needed or if DayPlanViewModel can be extended with a second uiState      \n ▎     stream for the “Today” tab.                                                                                    \n ▎                                                                                                                    \n ▎  If you want me to proceed with a detailed investigation and propose exact code changes, please let me know and    \n ▎  I’ll continue with a formal intent                                                               \n\nя не збираюсь прив'язувати для кожного окремого дня свій вміст панелі зв'язків. тому можна просто переписати логіку в dayPlanViewModel щоб вона віддавала контент панелі для всього Today Tab scope а не для кожного специфічного дня."
  },
